\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Five-fold trial-level cross-validated comparison of linguistic and phonetic/acoustic feature groups across anonymization systems and trial sets. The Text only, Phon./Acous. only, Combined, and + Int. columns report $R^2$ for \textbf {ASV score prediction}. Combined denotes the model using both text and phonetic/acoustic features. + Int. denotes the model with text, phonetic/acoustic features, and interaction terms. Best AUC reports the highest ROC-AUC obtained for target/non-target classification.}}{58}{table.caption.20}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Phonetic preservation features negatively correlated (Spearman) with speaker-level EER, by system and trial set. Negative correlations indicate that stronger preservation is associated with lower EER.}}{60}{table.11}%
